{% doc %}
  The store's WhatsApp link — the one place that reads the theme setting "מספר וואטסאפ"
  (contact_whatsapp). Prints `https://wa.me/<digits>` (plus `?text=` when a message is given),
  or nothing when there is no number; callers capture the output.
  The closing doc tag trims the newline after it: left-trimming the liquid tag instead leaves one
  newline (Shopify's whitespace trimming keeps it), which would start every captured value.
  The number is normalised by snippets/phone-href (spaces, dashes, dots, parentheses and "+"
  removed, a leading "00" dropped, a leading 0 — Israeli local format, 05x… — becomes 972), so
  the WhatsApp link and the tap-to-call links follow the same rules. `format: 'display'` prints
  the number for people instead: local format for Israeli numbers (053-3255020), "+<digits>"
  for others.

  @param {string} [text] - Pre-filled message as plain text (not HTML-escaped). URL-encoded here, spaces as %20 (WhatsApp shows "+" literally).
  @param {string} [format] - 'url' (default) or 'display'.
  @param {string} [phone] - Another WhatsApp number (e.g. a branch's). Default: the theme setting contact_whatsapp.

  @example
  {%- capture whatsapp_url -%}{% render 'whatsapp-url', text: settings.contact_whatsapp_message %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture whatsapp_display -%}{% render 'whatsapp-url', format: 'display' %}{%- endcapture -%}
{% enddoc -%}
{% liquid
  assign wa_phone = phone | strip | default: settings.contact_whatsapp
  capture wa_digits
    render 'phone-href', phone: wa_phone, format: 'e164'
  endcapture
  assign wa_digits = wa_digits | remove: '+'

  if wa_digits != blank
    if format == 'display'
      render 'phone-href', phone: wa_phone, format: 'display'
    else
      echo 'https://wa.me/' | append: wa_digits
      assign wa_text = text | strip | url_encode | replace: '+', '%20'
      if wa_text != blank
        echo '?text=' | append: wa_text
      endif
    endif
  endif
-%}
